---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { CARE_PLAN_FLOOR, CARE_PLAN_DEFAULT, FREE_BUILD } from '../config';
---

<Base
  title="Free build terms"
  description="The plain-English terms of the free website build: what's free, what's not, who owns what, and how handoff works."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <span class="eyebrow">Terms</span>
      <h1>The free build, in writing.</h1>
      <p class="lede" style="margin-top: var(--space-4);">
        This is the plain-English version of what we agree to before a build
        starts. You'll get it as a one-page document to sign — same content,
        no extra fine print.
      </p>

      <div class="stack" style="margin-top: var(--space-6);">
        <h2>What's free</h2>
        <p>
          One website with the pages your business needs, built from your
          intake answers — including custom functionality on the site where
          it helps, like quote forms and booking buttons. One revision
          round is included. First working draft within
          {FREE_BUILD.draftTimeline} of your confirmed slot — we confirm
          within one business day of intake, and if the month is full,
          you'll know then.
        </p>

        <h2>Revisions vs. bugs</h2>
        <p>
          A revision is a change of mind — structure, layout, what the site
          does. You get {FREE_BUILD.revisionRounds} revision round on the
          free build. A bug is something we built not working. Bug fixes
          are free for {FREE_BUILD.bugFixWindowDays} days after launch and
          never count against your revision — a bug we caused is never
          your bill.
        </p>

        <h2>What's not free</h2>
        <p>
          Standalone web apps (booking systems, portals, internal tools),
          ongoing edits and new content, photography and logo design, and
          ongoing growth services — all quoted plainly in writing if you
          want them, never assumed.
        </p>

        <h2>Ownership</h2>
        <p>
          You own the site. Your domain is registered in your own account
          from day one. At launch we transfer the code and hosting into
          accounts in your name, or host it for you on a care plan — your
          choice, changeable later.
        </p>

        <h2>Hosting</h2>
        <p>
          The build is free. Running any website costs hosting: roughly
          $0–20 a month if you run it yourself, or a care plan from
          {CARE_PLAN_FLOOR.price} if we handle it — {CARE_PLAN_DEFAULT.name}
          at {CARE_PLAN_DEFAULT.price} adds monthly content edits. Every
          plan cancels anytime: if you leave, we hand everything over
          within 5 business days at no charge.
        </p>

        <h2>Images and content</h2>
        <p>
          You confirm you have the right to use the photos, logos, and
          testimonials you give us. We only publish testimonials you have
          written permission to use.
        </p>

        <h2>Online payments (optional)</h2>
        <p>
          If you ask us to set up online payments — invoice payments,
          deposits, checkout — they run through your own Stripe account,
          connected to a payments platform operated by Long Hall Financial,
          Signalworks' parent company. Stripe's processing fees pass
          through unchanged; our platform share is disclosed in writing
          before the payment page goes live, and shown on the page itself.
          You can disconnect your Stripe account anytime and keep it.
        </p>

        <h2>What an "edit" is</h2>
        <p>
          On care plans, an edit is one request email covering up to three
          small changes to existing pages — hours, prices, photos, wording.
          New pages and redesign-scale changes are quoted in writing first.
          Unused edits don't roll over.
        </p>

        <h2>Our archive copy</h2>
        <p>
          We keep an archived copy of the finished site and may show the
          work as part of our portfolio. If you'd rather we didn't, say so
          and we won't.
        </p>

        <p class="muted" style="font-size: var(--text-sm);">
          Last updated: August 2026. The signed one-page agreement is the
          document that governs each build; this page is its plain-English
          twin and is kept in sync with it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
